【国家发展改革委、国家能源局关于"十五五"新型储能规划执行情况总结暨"十六五"规划编制工作阶段性进展通报】

为深入贯彻落实党中央、国务院关于新型储能高质量发展的决策部署,国家发展改革委、国家能源局近期组织开展了"十五五"新型储能规划执行情况系统总结,并全面启动"十六五"新型储能规划编制工作。现将有关情况通报如下:

一、"十五五"规划执行总体情况

1. 装机目标基本达成
- 累计并网装机(国家电网经营区):约332 GW;
- 在建项目(已签约EPC且开工):约82 GW;
- 加权可交付容量预估:约281 GW;
- 整体转换率(可交付/累计公告):约79%;
- 8小时以上长时段项目调度响应合规率:99.5%,与PJM长时资源99-100%信用区间持续对齐;
- 上半年累计清退不达标项目约5.6 GW,纳入失信名单项目:72个。

2. duration-stratified容量补偿机制执行成效
- 2-4小时、4-8小时、8小时以上三档定价机制运行平稳;
- 山东、浙江、青海、甘肃、新疆等省份开展动态持续时间分层认证机制试点;
- 试点机制引入与系统供需变化、辅助服务市场饱和度、可再生能源消纳压力挂钩的动态系数调整,变化幅度约束在±15%以内;
- weather zone/省级差异化权重设计提高容量价格信号精确性;
- 短时段(2小时以下)容量电价边际递减已成定势,资源正向长时段、可调度、高可用方向迁移;
- 4-8小时档项目调峰贡献度同比持续提高,8小时以上档项目调峰贡献度维持稳定。

3. "四可"功能刚性约束深化执行
- 各省级电网企业严格落实NEA《新型储能并网调度运行安全监管实施细则》要求;
- 按月报送调度运行数据,重点指标包括:等效利用小时数、调度响应合规率、连续可用时长、SOC一致性等;
- 容量电价与项目调度利用小时数、市场化调用率两项核心指标挂钩机制运行平稳;
- 年度调用率低于20%的项目按规定扣减容量电价;
- 多次不服从调度指令的项目纳入失信名单。

二、"十六五"规划编制重点

1. 配合NEA做好"十六五"新型储能规划编制工作,以习近平新时代中国特色社会主义思想为指导,深入贯彻党的二十大及历次全会精神;

2. 认真总结"十五五"经验,巩固中期评估成果,将全国长时段储能占比40%(2030年)、50%(2035年)的目标分解到具体项目;

3. 配合完善辅助服务市场产品体系,对持续时间长、响应精度高、调用可靠的长时段储能给予合理补偿;

4. 持续推进多元化技术路线商业化(压缩空气储能、液流电池、钠离子电池)、示范应用(固态电池、重力储能、热储能、氢储能)、研究探索(铁-空气电池、液态空气等前沿技术)三级分类推进机制;

5. 研究国际经验本土化适配
- 借鉴ERCOT Tier 4a/b/c(24-72小时、72-168小时、168小时以上)分级方法;
- 研究容量稀缺定价参数滚动校准机制(ORDC参数由季度调整为半年度);
- 长期容量合同与多日资源(100小时以上)双重定价机制。

三、关于国际经验借鉴

1. FERC Order No. 2023实施评估技术会议公告及会前评论程序值得关注。其六项议题(集群研究时间线缩减、退出与里程碑合规模式、容量认证整合、转化率披露作为透明度指标、长期运行记录与可融资性阈值、与州及ISO/RTO资源充足性规划的协调)对"十六五"规划编制具有重要参考价值;

2. ERCOT NPRR1240档位梯度约束方案征求意见稿(24小时以上档位细分为24-72h、72-168h、168+三档,accreditation factor均为1.00)系全球首个ISO/RTO将多日资源进一步细分至168+档的方案,值得深入研究;

3. DOE Liftoff第四波、第五波验证数据集所确立的"独立第三方验证+连续24个月以上运营记录"标准与NEA"四可"要求在底层逻辑上一致;

4. NESO Cap-and-Floor Control Period 2机制设计、SEC关于"已披露框架容量(如BYD组合的12.5 GWh)不等同于已投运容量"原则、MACSE"技术中立、竞争性采购、实际运行数据"原则,均对我国"十六五"规划编制具有重要参考价值;

5. 欧盟EU 2024/1711指令、Terna"已并网、已调度、可用容量、可用小时"披露口径、IEA《Global Energy Storage Project Conversion Database》四阶段口径(已签约EPC开工0.85、已招标未签约0.55、已签约未开工0.40、已宣布0.15),均对"十六五"规划编制具有重要参考价值。

四、下一步工作

1. 配合NDRC/NEA做好"十六五"新型储能规划编制,按要求完成本省"十六五"新型储能规划中期评估报告;

2. 持续深化动态duration-stratified容量电价机制,扩大试点范围;

3. 强化"四可"功能联调数据复核与按月上报机制,数据真实性纳入企业考核体系;

4. 配合做好新型储能并网调度运行安全监管实施细则落地,重点核查AGC/AVC联调、遥测接入、调度响应合规情况;

5. 持续深化国际技术交流,分享中国duration-stratified容量电价机制建设经验。

国家电网将继续坚持"安全底线、调度优先、市场导向"原则,以可验证的运行数据为基础,让储能真正成为新型电力系统的可靠调节资源。

【国家发展改革委 国家能源局关于新型储能高质量发展深化推进的指导意见——"十五五"阶段性总结与"十六五"前瞻部署】

各省(自治区、直辖市)发展改革委、能源局,国家电网公司、南方电网公司,有关行业协会和中央能源企业:

为深入贯彻落实党中央、国务院关于新型储能高质量发展的决策部署,认真做好"十五五"新型储能规划执行情况系统总结,科学谋划"十六五"新型储能规划编制工作,国家发展改革委、国家能源局就新型储能高质量发展深化推进提出以下指导意见。

一、"十五五"规划执行总体情况

1. 装机目标基本达成。截至2040年上半年,全国新型储能装机规模约332 GW,在建项目(已签约EPC且开工)约82 GW,加权可交付容量约281 GW,整体转换率(可交付/累计公告)约79%;长时段储能(4小时以上)占比稳步提升至40%以上,8小时以上长时段储能装机规模超过80 GW。

2. duration-stratified容量电价机制基本建立。三档定价机制(2-4小时、4-8小时、8小时以上)在山东、浙江、青海、甘肃、新疆等省份试点基础上全面推行;动态持续时间分层认证机制引入与系统供需变化、辅助服务市场饱和度、可再生能源消纳压力挂钩的动态系数调整,变化幅度约束在±15%以内;weather zone/省级差异化权重设计提高容量价格信号精确性。

3. "四可"功能刚性约束深化执行。各省级电网企业严格落实NEA《新型储能并网调度运行安全监管实施细则》要求,按月报送调度运行数据;累计清退不达标项目约5.6 GW,纳入失信名单项目72个;8小时以上长时段项目调度响应合规率达99.5%,与PJM长时资源99-100%信用区间持续对齐。

4. 多元化技术路线有序推进。压缩空气储能、液流电池、钠离子电池三类商业化重点技术规模化推广有序推进;固态电池、重力储能、热储能、氢储能处于示范应用阶段;铁-空气电池、液态空气等前沿技术处于研究探索阶段。

5. 转换率披露成为国际可比基础。按IEA《Global Energy Storage Project Conversion Database》四阶段口径(已签约EPC开工0.85、已招标未签约0.55、已签约未开工0.40、已宣布0.15)按技术路线×时长×辖区三维分布评估全国项目转化率。

二、"十六五"规划前瞻部署

1. 总体目标:到2030年新型储能装机规模超过300 GW、长时段储能占比不低于40%;到2035年装机规模超过500 GW、长时段储能占比不低于60%;到2040年装机规模稳步推进,长时段储能成为电力系统的基础设施和可调度资源。

2. 推进duration-stratified容量电价机制深化
- 巩固三档定价机制(2-4小时、4-8小时、8小时以上);
- 在既有静态三档基础上,研究引入更细颗粒度的"长时段"档位(8-24小时、24-72小时、72小时以上、168小时以上);
- 借鉴ERCOT Tier 4a/b/c分级方法,完善动态分层认证机制;
- 容量电价与项目调度利用小时数、市场化调用率两项核心指标直接挂钩,年度调用率低于20%的项目扣减容量电价;
- 多次不服从调度指令的项目纳入失信名单。

3. 配合做好多元化技术路线商业化
- 商业化重点:压缩空气储能、液流电池、钠离子电池;
- 示范应用:固态电池、重力储能、热储能、氢储能;
- 研究探索:铁-空气电池、液态空气等前沿技术;
- 各省级发展改革委、能源局要结合本地实际,将多元化技术路线作为重要发展方向。

4. 强化"四可"功能刚性约束
- 严格执行《新型储能并网调度运行安全监管实施细则》要求;
- 按月报送调度运行数据,重点指标包括:等效利用小时数、调度响应合规率、连续可用时长、SOC一致性等;
- 严守"四可"功能技术合规要求,对不达标项目限期整改并清退;
- 强化新型储能项目全生命周期监管,从核准、建设、并网、运行到退役实施全过程管理。

5. 持续深化国际合作
- 加强与FERC、AEMO、ERCOT、SECI、Terna、Ofgem/NESO、MACSE、IEA等国际同行的政策对话;
- 推进项目转化披露体系方法学互认;
- 推进多日可靠性指标(>24小时、>72小时、>168小时)工程参数对齐;
- 推进非锂长时商业化运行记录互认机制;
- 推进动态时长分层认证系数同行校准。

三、关于国际经验借鉴

1. PJM五年回顾、ERCOT NPRR1236动态分层认证、FERC Order No. 2023实施评估、SECI BESS项目转化率披露、MACSE长期容量合同、NESO Cap-and-Floor Control Period 2、Terna"已并网、已调度、可用容量、可用小时"披露口径、IEA《Global Energy Storage Project Conversion Database》四阶段口径、DOE Liftoff第三/四/五波验证数据集等,对我国"十六五"规划编制均具有重要参考价值;

2. SECI BESS-01运行数据(等效循环保留时长650-720次、SOC一致性98.5%以上、可用率96.2%以上)、Highview Power Carrington项目达到36个月连续运行记录、Form Energy商业参考机组100小时持续放电能力等,均为非锂长时商业化绑定性要求提供实证支撑;

3. 全球duration-stratified机制已从理论框架走向可比较、可验证、可融资的国际共识;FERC对PJM 2033/34 BRA的官方回应(4h级ICAP约75%、8h+约99-100%、首次大规模长时入市约3,400 MW)与NDRC中期评估在2040-H1同时出现,标志着这一基础架构从"倡议性共识"升级为"规划性基础设施"。

四、强化安全监管

1. 组织开展全国新型储能电站安全专项排查,重点排查电池热失控、消防设施、涉网保护等关键环节;

2. 对发现的问题坚决整改到位,守住安全底线;

3. 强化新型储能项目全生命周期监管,从核准、建设、并网、运行到退役实施全过程管理。

新型储能行业已进入高质量发展新阶段。我委将继续坚持"安全底线"与"高质量发展"并重,把新型储能真正建成电力系统可调度的基础设施资源,为构建以新能源为主体的新型电力系统提供有力支撑。展望2040年及更长时期,我们将以可验证的运行数据为基础,以技术中立为原则,以可调度可融资为目标,统筹推进新型储能在新型电力系统中发挥更大作用,为实现碳达峰碳中和目标作出更大贡献。

【ERCOT 2040-H2: Release of the NPRR1236 Three-Year Implementation Assessment and International Experience White Paper — End-of-Decade Strategic Statement】

ERCOT is publishing today, at the close of the 2040 horizon, the comprehensive NPRR1236 Three-Year Implementation Assessment and International Experience White Paper. This document consolidates operational evidence, methodology evolution, and cross-jurisdictional lessons learned from the period 2037-H1 through 2040-H1, and serves as ERCOT's end-of-decade strategic statement on duration-stratified market design.

1. Headline assessment findings

a) NPRR1236 dynamic accreditation has performed as designed:
   - 18 quarterly calibration cycles completed;
   - Average per-tier adjustment magnitude: 2.8% (range: 0.4% to 6.2%);
   - Zero retroactive changes to settled capacity payments;
   - Signal stability preserved while maintaining responsiveness to system-need changes.

b) Tier subdivision (24-72 / 72-168 / 168+ hour) has produced differentiated reliability signals:
   - Tier 4a (8-24 hour) average revenue: 0.91x 2022 baseline;
   - Tier 4b (72-168 hour) average revenue: 1.28x 2022 baseline;
   - Tier 4c (168+ hour) average revenue: 1.41x 2022 baseline for iron-air, 0.92x baseline for advanced compressed-air, 1.08x baseline for flow battery.

c) ORDC multi-day calibration has produced adequate scarcity signals:
   - 11 declared multi-day reserve events over three years;
   - Average scarcity rents for Tier 4b: $125-$165/kW-year;
   - Average scarcity rents for Tier 4c iron-air: $185-$225/kW-year.

d) Tier 4c forward reliability product: NOT NECESSARY based on IMM preliminary assessment. The merchant model with scarcity-based ORDC pricing has produced adequate investment signals for multi-day resources.

2. Six design principles that have held up

a) Technology-neutral accreditation. Duration tier determines value; technology is irrelevant to per-tier value.

b) Duration-stratified valuation. Physical reliability contribution during system stress windows is the binding metric.

c) Scarcity-based price signals. ORDC and energy/ancillary markets reveal system value; administrative capacity contracts are not the default.

d) Dynamic adjustment bounded by signal stability. Quarterly cadence with magnitude constraints has balanced responsiveness and investment-grade stability.

e) Operating-record evidence as the binding constraint. Independently verified performance data, not nameplate claims, determines accreditation and bankability.

f) Merchant model preservation. Where scarcity pricing produces adequate signals, scarcity pricing is the chosen mechanism; where it demonstrably fails, forward procurement may be evaluated but only on scarcity-based design.

3. International convergence

The White Paper documents the structural convergence that has emerged across major jurisdictions:

a) PJM (duration-weighted ICAP, annual cadence, BRA-based forward procurement);
b) ERCOT (NPRR1236 dynamic coefficients, semi-annual ORDC cadence, scarcity-based pricing);
c) NDRC/NEA (duration-stratified capacity pricing, three-tier mechanism, dynamic evolution);
d) AEMO (ISP duration-aware accreditation);
e) SECI (tender-to-commissioning conversion discipline, two-tier capacity compensation);
f) MACSE Italy (long-tenor capacity procurement for 8+ hour);
g) UK cap-and-floor (long-tenor revenue floor);
h) EU Network Code on Storage (forthcoming, duration-differentiated).

The methodological convergence reflects the principle that capacity payment must reflect availability, dispatch contribution, and duration value at point of interconnection, not nameplate registration.

4. What remains open as we enter the 2040s

a) Multi-day adequacy metrics beyond 24-hour stress windows. The 24-hour threshold in current LOLE calibration may be insufficient as renewable penetration continues to grow.

b) Dynamic accreditation cadence optimization. Annual versus semi-annual versus quarterly remains an open question; ERCOT's semi-annual ORDC cadence is a deliberate compromise.

c) Cross-jurisdictional data harmonization. The IEA Project Pipeline Database has provided methodological convergence, but operating-data disclosure practices still vary.

d) Technology evolution. Hydrogen-derived storage remains long-pathway; thermal storage and liquid-air storage are at varying stages of commercialization. The market design must remain technology-neutral while adapting to new operating-record evidence.

e) Bankability gap closure for non-lithium routes. SECI's 28% flow-battery share in the 6-hour tier demonstrates bankability at the upper end; iron-air and advanced compressed-air are approaching bankability at the multi-day tier.

5. ERCOT's institutional position — reaffirmed

ERCOT remains committed to competitive energy markets, scarcity-based price signals, and technology-neutral reliability standards. The merchant model has demonstrated that multi-day reliability can be revealed through scarcity pricing rather than purchased through administrative contracts.

The next decade will see continued evolution:
- LOLE calibration will extend to multi-day stress windows as the data supports it;
- ORDC calibration will continue semi-annual re-calibration with quarterly informational reports;
- Tier 4c operating record will be re-assessed annually;
- Cross-jurisdictional methodology convergence will continue through IEA, DOE national-lab studies, and bilateral technical exchange.

ERCOT will defend the design choices that have produced adequate investment signals. Where the evidence shows adjustment is needed, ERCOT will adjust parameters. Where the evidence shows the design is working, ERCOT will defend it against pressure to revert to administrative procurement.

6. Closing observation

The 2040 horizon closes with ERCOT having demonstrated that a state-level ISO, operating outside FERC wholesale-market jurisdiction, can design and operate a duration-stratified market that produces adequate investment signals across the full duration spectrum — from 2-hour ancillary services to 168+ hour multi-day reliability — through scarcity-based price signals, technology-neutral accreditation, and dynamic adjustment bounded by signal stability.

This is the ERCOT contribution to the global storage governance architecture: a working model of how merchant markets can integrate long-duration resources without resorting to administrative capacity procurement.

— ERCOT Market Operations & System Planning

